      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not define the frontal plane as the “side-to-side plane of the body.”",
        "The packet supports that dynamic balance during walking involves center of mass remaining within the base of support and that active balance control is especially focused on the frontal plane (contrast with sagittal plane), but the specific phrasing in the definition (“nervous system actively controls stability to keep the body’s center of mass within its base of support”) is more specific than what the packet explicitly states."
